---
/**
 * CardList
 *
 * The listing shell every card listing sits in: it owns the `<ul>` wrapper and
 * its layout, so call sites only map their items into `<li><Card/></li>` in the
 * default slot.
 *
 * It takes no options: every card listing on the site is drawn the same, so a
 * decision record and a case study carry the same heading rather than one
 * listing tightening its own. A listing that genuinely needs different cards
 * gets a new shell, not a flag here.
 *
 * Pages do not usually compose this directly: `EntryList` does, from a page's
 * array of items. Reach for it when a listing genuinely needs bespoke cards.
 *
 * @component
 *
 * @slot default - The `<li><Card/></li>` items.
 *
 * @example
 * ```astro
 * <CardList>
 *   {items.map((item) => <li><Card>...</Card></li>)}
 * </CardList>
 * ```
 */
---

<ul class="card-list">
  <slot />
</ul>

<style>
  .card-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--grid-padding);
  }
</style>
